ss></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISSAN CHEMICAL IND LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAGAWA MICHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIMIYA HIROFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUZAWA, HIROMITSU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUSHIMI, TAKAOMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISSAN CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAGAWA, MICHITO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIMIYA, HIROFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ARAI SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUZAWA HIROMITSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUSHIMI TAKAOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAGAWA MICHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIMIYA HIROFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUZAWA, HIROMITSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUSHIMI, TAKAOMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAGAWA, MICHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIMIYA, HIROFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A DNA being derived from a gene encoding rice adenylate kinase and exerting a promoter function in a plant body; a vector carrying the DNA having the promoter function; a bacterium containing the vector; a plant cell transformed by the vector; and a regenerated plant obtained from this cell and its seed. The above DNA having the promoter function can be ligated to a structural gene such as a reporter gene and integrated into a vector such as an expression vector. When the DNA having the promoter function is ligated to a vector together with a structural gene encoding a protein and a host plant is transformed thereby, the structural gene is expressed. Further, the expression of a desired structural gene can be regulated by ligating the desired gene under the control of the DNA fragment.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne, d'une part un fragment d'ADN dérivé d'un gène codant l'adénylate kinase du riz et exerçant une fonction de promoteur dans un corps végétal et d'autre part un vecteur portant l'ADN à fonction promoteur. L'invention concerne également une bactérie contenant le vecteur, une cellule végétale transformée par le vecteur, et une plante régénérée obtenue à partir de cette cellule et de sa semence. L'ADN à fonction promoteur de l'invention se prête, d'une part à la ligation sur un gène structurel tel qu'un gène rapporteur, et d'autre part à l'intégration à un vecteur tel qu'un vecteur d'expression. L'expression du gène structurel intervient dès lors que l'ADN à fonction promoteur dispose d'une ligation sur un vecteur alors qu'un gène structurel vient coder une protéine et qu'il en résulte une transformation d'une plante hôte. En outre, on peut réguler l'expression d'un gène structurel attendu par une ligation du gène attendu sous le contrôle du fragment d'ADN.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>